      "hints": [
        "Use $a = \\frac{\\text{Max}-\\text{Min}}{2}$ and $c = \\frac{\\text{Max}+\\text{Min}}{2}$.",
        "Find the period $T = \\pi$ and solve $T = \\frac{2\\pi}{b}$ for $b$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Determine the amplitude $a$ and vertical shift $c$ from the maximum $y = 8$ and minimum $y = -2$:\n$$a = \\frac{8 - (-2)}{2} = 5$$\n$$c = \\frac{8 + (-2)}{2} = 3$$",
        "Determine the frequency parameter $b$ from the period $T = \\pi$:\n$$T = \\frac{2\\pi}{b} = \\pi \\implies b = 2$$",
        "State the values of the constants:\n$$a = 5, \\quad b = 2, \\quad c = 3$$"
      ],
